    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n16295" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ēthos</span></b> , ĕos,
			n., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἦθος</span>. *
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Manners</i>, <i>morals</i>,
					<i><span class="en">Sid. Carm. 15,
			101</span></i>.—* </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A depicting of character.</i>—In <i>acc. plur.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ethē,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					35, 10, 36, § 98</span></i>
			; in <i>abl. plur.</i>: in ethesin Terentius
			poscit palmam, Varr. ap. <i><span class="en">Non. 374,
		9</span></i>.</div>
